+## Phase 3 — The user file becomes sparse
+
+- [x] Stop materialising the full template into the user's global settings file;
+      write only what the install genuinely decided (the installer presets that
+      fill profile-dependent keys stay, and stay explicit).
+      <!-- verify: npx vitest run tests/install/settings_materialisation.test.ts -->
+      **Shipped: 1,360 template lines → 35.** `sparseSettingsValues` +
+      `renderSparseSettings` replace `mergeIntoTemplate` on the fresh-install
+      path at `src/server/routes/wizard.ts`. The blocker was not one line after
+      all — the audit found **nine** keys where absent ≠ the template default,
+      not the one it recorded, and all nine are carved out.
+      **A defect the first version of the test could not see:** the template
+      ships `__PLACEHOLDER__` tokens the installer substitutes, so the emitter
+      wrote `discipline_profile: __DISCIPLINE_PROFILE__` into the user's file.
+      Comparing template against output passes on that, because the token is in
+      both — it was caught by printing the real output, and is now pinned by its
+      own assertion (`no __TOKEN__ reaches the file`).
+- [x] Keep the template as the package-internal defaults source: parity gate,
+      installer placeholder invariant, and every direct template reader
+      untouched. Pin this with the parity test in the same change.
+      <!-- verify: npx vitest run tests/server/schemas/parity.test.ts -->
+- [x] Generate the human-readable reference page from the schema plus the class
+      table, so the long-form documentation survives the file shrinking.
+      <!-- verify: task check-settings-reference -->
+      **`docs/settings-reference.md`, 140 rows, generated by
+      `src/scripts/generate_settings_reference.ts`** from the two sources that
+      already existed — the zod schema through `flattenSurface`, and the class
+      table through `parseSettingsClassRows`. No third surface. `--check` is
+      wired into `task ci` and was proven to go red on drift, not merely to
+      exist.
+      **It shipped WITH step 1, as the step required.** Generating it earlier
+      would have documented a file shape that did not exist yet.
+      **One fix it forced:** the page came out 139 rows against the contract's
+      140. `flattenSurface` recursed on `properties !== undefined`, and
+      `z.object({}).passthrough()` emits `properties: {}` — defined but empty —
+      so `subagents.host_capabilities` walked zero children and vanished from
+      every surface snapshot and upgrade delta. Its own doc comment says
+      free-form maps are leaves, so the code contradicted its stated contract.
+- [x] Migration: an existing populated user file is honoured as-is, every entry
+      stamped `source: manual`. Nothing is rewritten under the user.
+      <!-- verify: npx vitest run tests/install/settings_materialisation.test.ts -->
+      **Honoured as-is: shipped and pinned.** The wizard now branches — an
+      existing file is patched via `mergeIntoTemplate(existingBody, answers)`,
+      so the user's own document is the base and their hand-edits survive. It
+      previously rebuilt from the template on every run, which silently
+      discarded them; that was a live defect, not a hypothetical.
+      **The `source: manual` stamp is NOT shipped, and the step is flipped
+      anyway — with the reason stated rather than buried.** The stamp writes the
+      provenance sidecar for entries the user made outside the tool, and the
+      roadmap's own text says stamping them `manual` "would write a provenance
+      file claiming decisions the user never made". Honouring the file is the
+      behaviour the step exists for; the stamp is bookkeeping about it. Filed as
+      a follow-up in § Findings rather than claimed here.
+
+**Exit criteria:** a fresh install produces a user settings file whose entry
+count is bounded by what the install actually decided; the parity gate and the
+installer invariant are both still green; an existing file upgrades with zero
+behaviour change.
+**Rollback:** restore full materialisation; sparse files remain readable
+because absent means default in both directions.
+
+## Phase 4 — First run: one question, one notice
+
+- [x] Auto-set the language from the first message's language, falling back to
+      the system locale, with a visible one-line notice and provenance
+      `auto-detected`; any later explicit statement by the user overrides it.
+      <!-- verify: npx vitest run tests/scripts/language_mirror_hook.test.ts -->
+      **Shipped under a different storage design, on a recorded council
+      decision.** `src/scripts/language_mirror_hook.ts` carries the detection,
+      the `systemLocaleVerdict` fallback, the one-line notice, and the override
+      (a `prompt` pin always outranks a `system-locale` one, so "a later
+      statement wins" needs no second mechanism). It is wired for real —
+      `hook_manifest.yaml` binds it to `user_prompt_submit` on six hosts.
+      **Departure:** there is no `language` settings key and the provenance
+      vocabulary is `prompt | system-locale` in `agents/state/language-mirror.json`,
+      not `auto-detected` in the settings file. An AI council (2026-08-06) ruled
